<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Abdera</h1><p class="st-meta">800 BCE – 206 BCE (approx.) · capital Abdera</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Phoenician trading port on the coast of Almería, at modern Adra, that later minted coins under Carthaginian and Roman rule.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Phoenician settlers founded <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/abdera">Abdera</a> in the 8th century BCE on the hill of Montecristo at modern Adra, at the mouth of the river Adra. It was one of a chain of Phoenician harbours along the southern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sexi">Sexi</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/malaka">Malaka</a>, linking <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gadir">Gadir</a> with the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of its government. Like its neighbours, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/abdera">Abdera</a> lived from trade with the Iberian hinterland, fishing and the salting of fish. In the Punic period it fell under the influence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, and its later coins, inscribed in Punic letters, showed a temple facade with tuna fish.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the Roman victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> in 206 BCE <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/abdera">Abdera</a> came under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, keeping its coinage into the early empire. It continued as a small Roman town, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> listed it among the Phoenician foundations of the coast.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 800 BCE – 206 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54